<title>USA: General Instrument wins NYNEX work.</title>
<headline>General Instrument wins NYNEX work.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>NYNEX Corp said on Wednesday it selected NextLevel Communications, part of General Instrument Corp, to provide electronics for its new fiberoptic network in Boston and New York City.</p>
<p>No financial details were given, but the electronics will serve a minimum of one million new fiberoptic telephone lines, which are replacing copper cables as far as the curb.</p>
<p>NYNEX has an option to increase the contract to serve up to five million lines.</p>
<p>-- Nick Louth, New York Newsroom 212 859 1712</p>
</text>
